0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"study":{"id":"anvar","title":"The election record that had to be proved","category":"Landmark judgment","year":"2014","subtitle":"Anvar P.V. v. P.K. Basheer","fictional":false,"difficulty":"Electronic evidence","summary":"Electronic output required the special proof route under section 65B, rather than an unrestricted general secondary-evidence route.","story":["An election dispute involved recordings and media relied on to support allegations. The evidential question was not simply whether the material sounded persuasive: it was how electronic output could legally be proved.","The Supreme Court emphasized the special provision for electronic records. Anvar held that the general secondary-evidence rules could not bypass the conditions of section 65B for the output concerned.","The decision generated practical questions about certificates, original devices, and parties unable to control a source. Later decisions clarified the position. Today, the reasoning must be read with BSA section 63 and its Schedule rather than copied into a current filing unchanged."],"timeline":[{"date":"2014","event":"Supreme Court delivers the Anvar decision."},{"date":"2018","event":"Shafhi Mohammad introduces a relaxation later disapproved."},{"date":"2020","event":"Arjun Panditrao clarifies the certification position."},{"date":"2024","event":"BSA section 63 becomes the applicable new statutory framework."}],"issue":"The route for proving electronic-record contents under the former Evidence Act.","holding":"The special section 65B route governed the electronic output concerned. Current analysis must use the BSA and applicable precedent.","lessons":["Identify the exact output being tendered.","Distinguish original-device production from copied output.","Preserve source and process information early.","Read later clarifying judgments.","Update the certificate to the current Schedule."],"questions":["Why does admissibility require more than relevance?","What changed between the old certificate and BSA section 63?","How would you document a multi-device source?"],"sources":["anvar","arjun","bsa"],"topics":["2.9","2.10"]}}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/07qngb6s2_y2q.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
